  "explanation": "The question asks for the year Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus was elected consul. The sources D1S1, D1S2, D2S12, and D3S1 directly state that he was consul in 112 BC. The conflicting mention of 148 BC refers to a different individual with the same name (as noted in D1S1, D2S11, and D4S2), who was the father of the 112 BC consul. Since the question specifies Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (the one elected consul in 112 BC), the correct answer is 112 BC."
